    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>What should I do if I have been told I am blacklisted?</summary>
        <p>Contact us with what you know, including any notice or order you have received. We will review the basis for the blacklist and identify the appropriate procedural route to address it.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can FIS assist with a request to lift a blacklist entry?</summary>
        <p>Yes. FIS prepares and lodges the appropriate request, manages the filing and follow-through with the Bureau of Immigration, and keeps you informed as the matter progresses.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if I don't know exactly what record is attached to my name?</summary>
        <p>Tell us what you know. FIS can help establish what record or order is affecting you as part of the case assessment.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can FIS prepare and lodge a Motion for Reconsideration?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Where reconsideration is the appropriate remedy, FIS assesses the decision, prepares the motion and the supporting case, and lodges it on your behalf.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need to be in the Philippines for FIS to review my case?</summary>
        <p>No. FIS can review your case remotely using the immigration information, notices, records and supporting documents available to you. We can then prepare and manage the relevant motion, request or immigration process on your behalf.</p>
      </details>
